---
title: "Laplace approximation"
output: rmarkdown::html_vignette
vignette: >
  %\VignetteIndexEntry{Laplace approximation}
  %\VignetteEngine{knitr::rmarkdown}
  %\VignetteEncoding{UTF-8}
---

```{r, include = FALSE}
knitr::opts_chunk$set(collapse = TRUE, comment = "#>")
```

`lmm_animal_laplace()` and `lm_phen_cov_laplace()` fit the same models as the
samplers by a Laplace approximation: a Gaussian at the mode on the unconstrained
scale, with draws from it transformed to the reported quantities. It is not a
posterior sample. There are no MCMC diagnostics, and the draw-based tools
(`fit_draws()`, `fit_loo()`, `breeding_values()`, `posterior_predictive()`,
`imputed_data()`) refuse the result. Use it to explore, then confirm with the
sampler.

This vignette compares the two on the same simulated phenotypic data.

```{r packages, message = FALSE}
library(stanimal)
```

```{r simulate}
set.seed(2026)
n <- 200
X <- cbind(intercept = 1, predictor = rnorm(n))
P <- matrix(c(1, 0.4, 0.4, 1.5), 2)
Y <- X %*% rbind(c(0.5, -0.5), c(0.3, -0.2)) +
  matrix(rnorm(n * 2), n) %*% chol(P)
colnames(Y) <- c("trait1", "trait2")
```

```{r fit, message = FALSE}
approx <- lm_phen_cov_laplace(Y, X, draws = 2000, seed = 41)
sampled <- lm_phen_cov(Y, X, iter = 1000, warmup = 500, chains = 2,
                       cores = 2, seed = 41, refresh = 0)
```

```{r compare}
approx
sampled$summary(c("P", "corrP"))[, c("variable", "mean", "sd", "rhat")]
sampled$diagnostic_summary()
```

Agreement here does not guarantee agreement in other models. Skewed or
multimodal posteriors are approximated poorly, particularly for variances and
heritabilities, whose standard deviations are the least reliable entries of the
approximation.
